WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.930 line:92%
- My next guest is an award-winning fashion designer

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.700 line:92%
and one of Time Magazine's 100 most influential people.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.240 line:92%
Recently he's taken his talent

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.230 line:92%
to the front lines of the pandemic.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.770 line:92%
I'm happy to call him a friend, Christian Siriano, y'all.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:13.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How you doing?

00:00:13.736 --> 00:00:14.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Let me tell ya.

00:00:14.569 --> 00:00:15.402 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(sighs)

00:00:15.402 --> 00:00:16.235 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's tough.

00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:17.993 line:92%
(Kelly laughing) but doing good, doing good.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.080 line:92%
- But the world has changed a bit

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.190 line:92%
since we last saw each other so,

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:26.430 line:92%
how are you staying sane in all of this?

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.270 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah, I know.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.570 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's been wild.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:29.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It really has.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.140 line:92%
I mean, I live in New York which is really,

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.530 size:75% position:38% line:92%
got hit pretty hard.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.114 line:92%
And it's a weird place, to see everything closed

00:00:37.114 --> 00:00:39.817 line:92%
and it's kind of wild and,

00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:43.400 line:92%
but I've listening to the Governor, kind of everyday

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.560 line:92%
and there were such like a shortage of things,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.990 line:92%
and I was like, "Well, maybe I can do something."

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.360 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So that's kind of like,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.340 line:92%
why I started just kinda pitching in.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.890 line:92%
I felt like maybe we can help.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:55.870 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And that was kind of it.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.930 line:92%
I just felt like I couldn't just sit at home and do nothing.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:00.420 size:81% position:41% line:92%
- It's so devastating.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.880 line:92%
Like you're in a very devastating area

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.270 size:81% position:41% line:92%
with this whole virus.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.560 line:92%
And you know, it's really cool though.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.080 line:92%
I just wanted to say thank you

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.020 line:92%
because you could just be chilling and doing nothing.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:11.853 line:92%
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:11.853 --> 00:01:13.510 line:92%
You could just be relaxing and like, a lot of people

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.560 line:92%
are just like, "Okay, I'm just gonna stay safe and healthy."

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.600 line:92%
And you heard a need for something

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.270 line:92%
and then used your talent for this,

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.780 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and it's super cool.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.070 line:92%
And I just wanted to say thank you for doing that,

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.730 line:92%
for something, you know, like,

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.090 line:92%
everybody doing something matters.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.740 line:92%
So, what is the process though, of making masks?

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.130 line:92%
'Cause that's very different from dresses and outfits.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.560 line:92%
(Christian laughing) So, I'm like, yes.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.840 line:92%
Is that hard or is it weird?

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.870 line:92%
- It's like wild, it's like wild.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.020 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I mean, I literally,

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.570 line:92%
after like I tweeted at the Governor and they responded,

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.040 line:92%
you know, they give us kind of permission to open my office

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.430 line:92%
with a small team and I realized you know,

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.450 line:92%
my sewers are like couture sewers.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.950 line:92%
And now, they're like making masks.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.750 line:92%
It's quite monotonous work.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.660 line:92%
It's the same thing over and over again.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.300 line:92%
And at the beginning, we were only making like, white.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.380 line:92%
And now, I was like, we need to have some color,

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.870 line:92%
like I need something because we've done almost

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.600 line:92%
15,000 masks and you're like, "Oh, my God."

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.770 size:81% position:41% line:92%
- [Kelly] "Oh my God."

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.250 line:92%
- Your eyes are like bulging out

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.860 line:92%
because it's the same thing.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.760 line:92%
And it's kind of hard to make quality control

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.340 line:92%
when you, you know, I didn't have a mask factory.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:16.100 line:92%
And, I just kinda turned it into one, so,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's kind of wild.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.770 line:92%
- Yeah, because there are like, I guess, specifications

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.770 line:92%
in what the mask has to be able to do

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:22.603 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and the filtration.

00:02:22.603 --> 00:02:23.520 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.900 line:92%
We've looked at it too, because I quilt

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.860 line:92%
and I've thought of doing it with my five year old,

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.180 line:92%
like on our little sewing machine here,

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.357 line:92%
and just start to make stuff, and I was like,

00:02:30.357 --> 00:02:32.840 line:92%
"Oh gosh, I gotta figure out all how to do that."

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.717 line:92%
I was like, "It's so crazy different."

00:02:33.717 --> 00:02:36.490 line:92%
- You got a sewing machine and it's really hard.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.510 line:92%
- Oh my gosh, it's so difficult.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:39.580 line:92%
But it's really cool though that y'all are doing that.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.780 line:92%
But, so, and I actually love that you did the color

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.210 line:92%
and you added the color because I know that seems like

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:48.575 line:92%
a silly thing but we could use color right now.

00:02:48.575 --> 00:02:51.010 line:92%
And such a black and white scenario,

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.370 line:92%
like color can make people happy.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:55.330 line:92%
Like when I see the color yellow, it helps me.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.460 line:92%
When I see the color, you know, rich, vibrant colors,

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.293 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it just helps me.

00:02:58.293 --> 00:02:59.840 line:92%
So I think that's actually smart.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.540 line:92%
I know it seems silly but, it's not.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.270 line:92%
- No, but like, even the women in my office,

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:06.930 line:92%
who are like working everyday who still like,

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.780 line:92%
have a job, and like feed their families,

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.540 line:92%
they feel different when they're like,

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.210 line:92%
making a fuschia masks all day

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.740 line:92%
instead of just a plain, gray one.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.970 line:92%
Like, you can tell in their face, you know?

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.500 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Which is really nice.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.380 line:92%
- Yeah, I mean, this is kind of cool too,

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.580 line:92%
just as a business owner.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.260 line:92%
I mean you run a business and you families like, you know?

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.100 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And they need to be fed,

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.820 line:92%
and so, it's kind of a difficult position for a lot

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.210 line:92%
of owners of businesses because their income

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:30.785 line:92%
really isn't coming in so it's like,

00:03:30.785 --> 00:03:33.750 line:92%
is this kind of a way you thought would be cool to kind of

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.760 line:92%
keep them going and then also help out the community?

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.287 line:92%
- Yeah, it's like the best of both worlds.

00:03:39.287 --> 00:03:41.080 line:92%
We get to send thousands of things

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.120 line:92%
to hospitals, like kind of around the US which is amazing,

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.100 line:92%
and then, also, my seamstresses,

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.270 line:92%
my pattern makers, everybody that works my office,

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.700 line:92%
who have five kids, some of them,

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.760 line:92%
they get to still keep their job,

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.960 line:92%
and that was what I was actually so scared about.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.940 line:92%
I was like, "What can we do?"

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:57.773 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We make clothes.

00:03:57.773 --> 00:04:00.000 line:92%
We don't sit at home and work on the internet.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.900 line:92%
We make something everyday so we have to go and do it.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.740 line:92%
- It's clever and it's helpful.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.840 line:92%
So how can people help you?

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:08.900 line:92%
Like with the work you're doing.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.400 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Can anybody help or?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:14.020 line:92%
We just been having everybody go to christiansiriano.com.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.480 line:92%
We have like everything there

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.990 line:92%
like information, how you can help,

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.610 line:92%
or even if people wanna like, help their friends

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.910 line:92%
by making masks, so all that's on the website, yeah.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:23.743 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- That's awesome.

00:04:23.743 --> 00:04:26.530 line:92%
What's your personal version of PJ's till noon,

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:27.870 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
quarantine fashion?

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:28.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:28.703 --> 00:04:31.820 line:92%
It's really funny because I have noticed,

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.860 line:92%
like I'm really into like everybody in their looks

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.590 line:92%
and like, I loved the pillow challenge.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:36.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I think it's chic.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.060 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I get dressed everyday.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:42.010 line:92%
Like I wear jeans and you know, and I like need to

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.260 line:92%
because otherwise, then I won't do anything.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.630 line:92%
I really will be lazy and I can't.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.240 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I have to keep active.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.073 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:50.073 --> 00:04:52.668 line:92%
I am able to conquer the world in pajama pants.

00:04:52.668 --> 00:04:55.080 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.010 line:92%
- Honestly that's talent, that's talent!

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.140 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- It is a talent.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm so talented.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.320 line:92%
Well, have you seen any quarantine fashion

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:04.790 line:92%
on social media that you love?

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:05.623 line:92%
You mentioned the pillow thing.

00:05:05.623 --> 00:05:07.090 size:88% position:44% line:92%
What's the pillow thing?

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:09.010 line:92%
- The pillow challenge is where you take your pillow

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:10.310 line:92%
and you basically belt it, and you like,

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.300 size:81% position:41% line:92%
make a gown out of it.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.187 line:92%
You have to look up Halle Berry's.

00:05:12.187 --> 00:05:13.047 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:13.047 --> 00:05:13.880 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- I love it.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.210 line:92%
- Halle Berry's is so fabulous.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.420 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's amazing.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.230 line:92%
- So, one thing I did want to ask is

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.670 line:92%
I saw this when you first came on

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:22.503 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and I saw the video,

00:05:22.503 --> 00:05:24.050 line:92%
there's like so many drawings behind you.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.190 line:92%
So are you like, are you just drawing?

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.410 line:92%
Are you creating like crazy?

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.850 line:92%
'Cause a lot of, I've been writing like crazy, as an artist.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.750 line:92%
So, have you just been drawing like nonstop?

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:36.430 line:92%
- It's like my self-care is like, painting and sketching

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:39.240 line:92%
and like, that's like, my little escapism.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.930 line:92%
I actually, just you know, while I'm here.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.690 line:92%
Well, I did a happy birthday present for you,

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:49.050 line:92%
and I sketched you our three favorite looks.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:52.220 line:92%
This is granny, Golden Globes, and "Trolls" premiere,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.320 line:92%
and these are my gift to you.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.580 line:92%
I'm sorry they're not framed

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.290 line:92%
because my framer clearly isn't working.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.031 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh my gosh!

00:05:58.031 --> 00:05:59.740 line:92%
- For you. - That's so nice!

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:01.360 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Happy birthday!

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.450 line:92%
- I love those, I remember that one!

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.050 line:92%
I felt like Lucy in "Game of Thrones".

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I felt so cool.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.031 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I love those.

00:06:08.031 --> 00:06:09.923 line:92%
Thank you so much, that's so kind!

00:06:09.923 --> 00:06:10.773 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- You're welcome!

